ugh 1964. Points were awarded in each race based on placement in the race and the number of boats racing. The worst of a boat’s seven scores were eliminated, thus using the best six of seven scores for the final total."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Unusually there were two sites for 1952 yachting, with the Finn class raced off Liuskasaari, an island south of Helsinki, and the home of Helsingfors Segelsällskap, the second oldest sailing club in Finland. The other four events were held off the coast of Harmaja, an island outside of Helsinki, just south of the Suomenlinna sea fortress."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Nine nations won medals in 1952, with four nations winning the five events. The United States won two gold medals, and three medals in all, with Norway and Sweden also winning three medals."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/9538"} "One Person Dinghy (Finn), Open"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "20 – 28 July 1952"] "\n" [:td {} "28"] "\n" [:td {} "28"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/9551"} "Two Person Keelboat (Star), Open"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "20 – 28 July 1952"] "\n" [:td {} "42"] "\n" [:td {} "21"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/9564"} "Three Person Keelboat (Dragon), Open"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "20 – 28 July 1952"] "\n" [:td {} "51"] "\n" [:td {} "17"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/9577"} "5.5 metres, Open"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "20 – 28 July 1952"] "\n" [:td {} "50"] "\n" [:td {} "16"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/9590"} "6 metres, Open"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "20 – 28 July 1952"] "\n" [:td {} "56"] "\n" [:td {} "11"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {}] "\n" [:td